  "description": "The self- containment of the 1st and 2nd floor flats, incorporating a rear roof extension with door, external staircase and balustrade and roof lights to the front roof of the house.",
  "site_name": "47",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "21/08/2006",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": "Chiswick High Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major all other major developments",
  "lapsed_date": "09/08/2009",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - The flat roof area to the rear of the upper floor flat shall not be used as a balcony, roof garden or similar amenity area without the grant of further specific permission from the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 5 - The development consisting of the self-containment of the first and second floor flats, and the erection of a rear roof extension and external staircase, and the installation of two roof lights to the front roof of the building, as shown on drawing numbers 719/01, 719/03, 719/04 and 719/06 received 27 June 2006, is satisfactory as the upper floors of the building were in use for many years as two flats and the proposal would not unduly detract from the appearance of the building or street scene and would maintain the existing amenity of neighbouring residents. Therefore the proposed development is consistent with the relevant London Borough of Hounslow Unitary Development Plan 2003 policies; ENV-B.1.1 New Development, and H.6.4 Extensions and Alterations and the Supplementary Planning Guidance."
  ],
